tags: price-bound, price_bounded, price_volatility

A promise of the node: a bound on the growth of the price of an instance, counted from
its launch.

The value is key=value lines, sorted by key: num and den (the growth v as num/den, num
of 0 or more, den of 1 or more) and period (T, seconds, 0 or more). Example: den=10,
num=1 and period=86400, one on each line. In the period k of the instance (k = floor(
seconds since the launch / T) + 1; k = 1 when T is 0), the price of each resource is
at most floor(P * (num+den)^k / den^k), where P is its price at the launch. It is also
never more than the promise scarcity-max allows. A fall of the price is not limited.

With no promise, the price can grow with no bound. The node is bound.

